  "published": "2026-08-04",
  "insights": [
   "The market has undergone a significant technical reset in July, characterized by retail deleveraging, reduced market concentration, and normalized funding conditions.",
   "Retail investors shifted from buying weakness to reducing exposure, with the largest week of retail equity selling since 2022 occurring in late July.",
   "Technology and semiconductor sectors saw record retail liquidations, with semiconductor-focused leveraged ETF assets down ~55% from June peaks.",
   "Corporate buyback demand is set to reaccelerate significantly as earnings blackout windows expire, with 85% of S&P 500 market cap eligible for repurchases by mid-August.",
   "Earnings growth expectations for Q2 have surged from 22.4% to ~45%, with valuations in the IT sector compressing to 1st percentile levels (20x forward earnings)."
  ],
